<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd Rabbuh Mansur Hadi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd Rabbuh Mansur Hadi is a Yemeni politician who was vice-president under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-abdullah-saleh">Ali Abdullah Saleh</a> from 1994 and became president in 2012, after the 2011 uprising forced Saleh to hand over power. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/houthi-movement">Houthis</a> seized Sanaa in 2014 and he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> and then Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, prompting the Saudi-led intervention of 2015. In 2022 he transferred his powers to a Presidential Leadership Council.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abd-rabbuh-mansur-hadi.jpg" alt="Abd Rabbuh Mansur Hadi" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S Defense Department · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdrabbuh_Mansur_Hadi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
